1
00:04:43,448 --> 00:04:49,448
Being the adventures of a young man whose principal
interests are rape, ultra-violence and Beethoven.

2
00:09:26,896 --> 00:09:32,896
A Clockwork Orange is a science fiction, crime film directed by Stanley Kubrick.

3
00:14:10,344 --> 00:14:16,344
In a near-future Britain, young Alexander DeLarge and his pals get
their kicks beating and raping anyone they please.

4
00:18:53,793 --> 00:18:59,793
When not destroying the lives of others, Alex swoons to the music of Beethoven.

5
00:23:37,241 --> 00:23:43,241
The state, eager to crack down on juvenile crime, gives an incarcerated Alex the option
to undergo an invasive procedure that'll rob him of all personal agency.

6
00:28:20,689 --> 00:28:26,689
In a time when conscience is a commodity, can Alex change his tune?

7
00:33:04,137 --> 00:33:10,137
Alex, played by Malcolm McDowell.

8
00:37:47,586 --> 00:37:53,586
Mr. Alexander, played by Patrick Magee.

9
00:42:31,034 --> 00:42:37,034
Dr. Brodsky, played by Carl Duering.

10
00:47:14,482 --> 00:47:20,482
Chief Guard, played by Michael Bates.

11
00:51:57,931 --> 00:52:03,931
Dim, played by Warren Clarke.

12
00:56:41,379 --> 00:56:47,379
Georgie, played by James Marcus.

13
01:01:24,827 --> 01:01:30,827
A Clockwork Orange is a 1971 dystopian crime film written,
produced, and directed by Stanley Kubrick.

14
01:06:08,275 --> 01:06:14,275
It is based on Anthony Burgess's 1962 novel.

15
01:10:51,724 --> 01:10:57,724
The film employs disturbing and violent themes to comment on psychiatry, juvenile delinquency, youth
gangs, and broader social, political, and economic issues in a dystopian near-future Britain.

16
01:15:35,172 --> 01:15:41,172
Alex (Malcolm McDowell), the central character, is a charismatic, anti-social delinquent whose interests include
classical music (especially that of Beethoven), committing rape, theft, and "ultra-violence".

17
01:20:18,620 --> 01:20:24,620
He leads a small gang of thugs, Pete (Michael Tarn), Georgie (James Marcus), and Dim (Warren Clarke),
whom he calls his droogs (from the Russian word друг, which is "friend", "buddy").

18
01:25:02,068 --> 01:25:08,068
The film chronicles the horrific crime spree of his gang, his capture, and attempted rehabilitation via an experimental
psychological conditioning technique (the "Ludovico Technique") promoted by the Minister of the Interior (Anthony Sharp).

19
01:29:45,517 --> 01:29:51,517
Alex narrates most of the film in Nadsat, a fractured adolescent slang composed of
Slavic languages (especially Russian), English, and Cockney rhyming slang.

20
01:34:28,965 --> 01:34:34,965
The film premiered in New York City on 19 December 1971 and was
released in the United Kingdom on 13 January 1972.

21
01:39:12,413 --> 01:39:18,413
The film was met with polarised reviews from critics and was
controversial due to its depictions of graphic violence.

22
01:43:55,862 --> 01:44:01,862
After it was cited as having inspired copycat acts of violence, the film was withdrawn from
British cinemas at Kubrick's behest, and it was also banned in several other countries.

23
01:48:39,310 --> 01:48:45,310
In the years following, the film underwent a critical
re-evaluation and earned a cult following.

24
01:53:22,758 --> 01:53:28,758
It received several awards and nominations, with four nominations
at the 44th Academy Awards, including Best Picture.

25
01:58:06,206 --> 01:58:12,206
In the British Film Institute's 2012 Sight & Sound polls of the world's greatest films, A
Clockwork Orange was ranked 75th in the directors' poll and 235th in the critics' poll.

26
02:02:49,655 --> 02:02:55,655
In 2020, the film was selected for preservation in the United States National Film Registry by the
Library of Congress as being "culturally, historically, or aesthetically significant".

27
02:07:33,103 --> 02:07:39,103
The film explores themes of london, england, robbery, street
gang, great britain, based on novel or book.

28
02:12:16,551 --> 02:12:22,551
The tone is dark and thought_provoking and intense.
